From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: the ASTC opacity scan reads 16 KiB at a time by default (waveydude's 0917), unconditional crash fix; EDEN_UP_ASTC_SCAN_CHUNKS=0 is the old scan

What: JoinImages decides whether a new ASTC image is opaque (re-packed as BC1, half of BC3) by
reading the whole image, up to 64 MiB, into astc_scan_buffer, a vector that grows to the largest
image seen and is kept. waveydude's crash 20261111-095523: operator new refused 32,435,200 bytes for
that resize on the GPU back thread. 0579 (T137) already ported his 0917 loop, but only with
EDEN_UP_ASTC_SCAN_CHUNKS=1, which our play settings do not set.

Now the chunked scan (16 KiB pieces through the fixed astc_scan_chunk, stop at the first block with
alpha) is the default. EDEN_UP_ASTC_SCAN_CHUNKS: unset or any other text = chunked; exactly "0" =
the old whole-image scan (a way back for a comparison); exactly "2" = verify, as in 0579. The
"EDEN_UP_ASTC_SCAN_CHUNKS 10s:" line now prints only when the switch is set to exactly 1 or 2, so
the default adds no log line.

Why unconditional: IsOpaque (textures/astc.cpp) judges each whole 16-byte block on its own, skips a
partial tail and returns false at the first block with alpha; 16 KiB is a whole number of blocks and
each piece starts on a block, so the pieces cover the same blocks and the answer is the same for
every image (host check: the real IsOpaque, 2,606 images up to 32,435,200 bytes, 0 differences).
What changes: no heap request at scan time, fewer guest bytes read for images with alpha, and the
scan buffer no longer holds up to 64 MiB of heap after a big scan.

Origin and credit: waveydude, patch 0917 ("Scan ASTC opacity with fixed-size scratch"), commit
c405b1f; the loop is his (as placed by 0579).
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index b58ec3f..1e16e2d 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -6176,13 +6176,21 @@ ImageId TextureCache<P>::JoinImages(const ImageInfo& info, GPUVAddr gpu_addr, DA
                 // blocks are 16 bytes and IsOpaque judges each on its own, and 16 KiB is a whole
                 // number of blocks, so the answer is the same. 2 = verify: the chunked scan runs,
                 // then the old whole-image scan, whose answer is used; differences are counted.
-                // Unset: a few tests of one static int, then the old path below, unchanged.
+                // 0661 (T149): the chunked scan is the default. Unset, or anything but exactly
+                // "0" or "2", is mode 1; "0" is the old whole-image scan (a way back for a
+                // comparison). Same answer either way (above), so a crash fix with no switch; the
+                // 10 s line below only when EDEN_UP_ASTC_SCAN_CHUNKS is set to exactly 1 or 2.
                 static const int scan_chunks = [] {
                     const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_ASTC_SCAN_CHUNKS");
                     if (value == nullptr || value[0] == '\0' || value[1] != '\0') {
-                        return 0;
+                        return 1;
                     }
-                    return value[0] == '1' ? 1 : value[0] == '2' ? 2 : 0;
+                    return value[0] == '0' ? 0 : value[0] == '2' ? 2 : 1;
+                }();
+                static const bool scan_chunks_log = [] {
+                    const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_ASTC_SCAN_CHUNKS");
+                    return value != nullptr && (value[0] == '1' || value[0] == '2') &&
+                           value[1] == '\0';
                 }();
                 bool chunked_opaque = true;
                 if (scan_chunks != 0) {
@@ -6223,7 +6231,7 @@ ImageId TextureCache<P>::JoinImages(const ImageInfo& info, GPUVAddr gpu_addr, DA
                     }
                 }
                 ++(new_info.astc_opaque ? astc_opaque_images : astc_alpha_images);
-                if (scan_chunks != 0) {
+                if (scan_chunks_log) {
                     const auto now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
                     if (astc_chunk_last_log == std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point{}) {
                         astc_chunk_last_log = now;
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
index 02918dc..b005dd2 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
@@ -372,7 +372,8 @@ class TextureCache : public VideoCommon::ChannelSetupCaches<TextureCacheChannelI
     u64 astc_alpha_images{};
     std::vector<u8> astc_scan_buffer;
     /// EDEN_UP_ASTC_SCAN_CHUNKS (waveydude 0917): fixed scan piece, part of the cache object (no
-    /// heap request at scan time), and the 10 s line's counters. Unused while the switch is unset.
+    /// heap request at scan time), and the 10 s line's counters. Used by default since 0661
+    /// (EDEN_UP_ASTC_SCAN_CHUNKS=0 goes back to astc_scan_buffer).
     std::array<u8, 16 * 1024> astc_scan_chunk;
     u64 astc_chunk_scans{};
     u64 astc_chunk_read_bytes{};
